      "advisory_ids": [
        "RUSTSEC-2026-0293"
      ],
      "rationale": "Accepted by Donald on 2026-09-22. songbird 0.6.0 (the voice driver) depends on ringbuf \"0.4\" (its Cargo.toml [dependencies.ringbuf] version = \"0.4\"), so the fixed ringbuf 0.5.2 is not semver-compatible and cannot be selected without a songbird release. The advisory's double free needs an element whose Drop panics inside Consumer::skip or Consumer::clear. songbird's only ring buffer is the async input adapter's SharedRb<Heap<u8>> (HeapProd<u8>/HeapCons<u8> in src/input/adapters/async_adapter.rs, which calls rb.skip on seek), and u8 has no Drop, so the precondition cannot occur in this build. abbey-bot itself does not use ringbuf.",
      "review_triggers": [
        "songbird releases a version that depends on ringbuf >=0.5.2, or the songbird -> ringbuf edge changes.",
        "songbird's ring buffer element type stops being u8, or songbird adds another ringbuf consumer.",
        "abbey-bot takes a direct ringbuf dependency.",
        "The dependency topology, package source, version, or checksum changes.",
        "Any accepted advisory fingerprint changes or a vulnerability appears or disappears."
